WEBVTT

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:04.280
Alice, I want you to become 
the vocalist of In NO Hurry.

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:10.230
On May 29th, I want you to perform with 
us on the live <i>Music King</i> broadcast.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.570
But Yuzu, that day...

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.940
I'm going to the audition.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.940
You can do it after the audition.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:24.960
Even if I know I'll fail, it seems 
I'm just no good at giving up, Yuzu.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.130
Same here, Alice.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:31.850
<i>That day, we who were 
hiding how we truly felt</i>

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:33.660
<i>joined hands.</i>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:38.930
– 3 Years Ago –

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.930
You're a pretty awful singer,

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:40.120
aren't you?

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:40.930
Yeah.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.720
But your songs are really good.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.350
They're all very high-quality 
and stick with you.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.330
You sing here every day, right?

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.150
I always thought that was nice 
and had to wonder about you.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.190
You've got a lot of songs. 
Are you hoping to go pro?

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.700
I want to make money.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:00:59.620
To pay for school?

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.500
I want to do something 
about my parents' debt.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.490
My name's Kuze Tsukika. You?

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.500
Sakaki Momo.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.020
Is this all of them?

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.490
Yes. That's all the songs 
I've written recently.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.440
They're good. They work perfectly 
for the genre, and they're fun.

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:32.360
But why are they all in a 
key for a woman's voice?

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.600
There's no real reason.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:38.200
Jam with the jan-re, please.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:41.420
It was a pun.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:42.610
You're supposed to laugh.

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:44.260
Pass.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:45.500
My pun does?

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:46.210
No.

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:49.630
Sakaki-kun, can you write 
a song by tomorrow?

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:53.170
We have an idol group called Baby.

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:56.320
Their first and second singles bombed, 
and now their backs are against the wall.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.680
If their next one fails, 
the group will be disbanded.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.400
We'll never find a songwriter willing 
to board a sinking ship like this.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.600
I managed to get one song written for them,

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:08.050
but I don't think it's likely to sell too well.

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:10.350
Will this make me money if I do it?

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.930
It will. If it sells.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:17.540
Can I change my name?

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:18.340
Sure.

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:21.950
If it does sell well, I refuse to 
have any dealings with the press.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.200
That's fine.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:24.700
I'll do it.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:28.320
If it'll make me money, 
I can write any kind of song.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:29.650
Are you sure?

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:33.090
Haven't you been writing 
these songs for someone?

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:35.090
It's fine.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:38.500
I'll never see her again anyway.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:16.000
♭05 I Wouldn't Have Had to See You Smile Like That

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:15.840
<i>When I shout, that alone makes me invincible</i>

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:19.510
<i>So please don't open this—</i>

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:20.480
Stop!

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.220
Time to stop.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:25.410
Sheesh. You've got a long way 
to go with the fundamentals.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:28.830
Didn't you have Miou teaching you?

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.250
So do a better job of keeping it together.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.250
I'll keep that in mind.

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:37.140
Can I drink this Yapult?

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:38.420
What?!

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.960
You should only drink one 
a day! That's your second!

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.840
Haruyoshi-senpai, you're going off-topic.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:46.390
He's right.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:49.550
I don't care about your intake of 
the probiotic L. casei Shirota.

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:51.060
It's the way you project your voice!

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:54.390
True, but she's better than 
the first time she sang with us.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:57.320
You were atrocious back then, Nino-chan!

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:01.210
He really cuts deep without a second thought.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:02.360
Really, it was just so, so bad!

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.360
That's scary.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:05.980
Yana, do you know any 
available vocal teachers?

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:07.770
All right, leave it to me.

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:09.870
Yana-san, thank you very much.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:13.560
Don't thank me. I'm only thinking 
about In NO Hurry's welfare.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.870
By the way, Haruyoshi-senpai...

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:20.870
The proper full name of that bacteria 
is Lactobacillus casei Shirota.

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:21.840
I know that!

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:24.510
What happened to her conversation with me?

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:28.270
Give it up, Yana. Alice basically 
doesn't listen to anyone.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:31.290
So you're giving me another 
difficult person to handle, then?

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:34.430
The costumes for your new song are all ready!

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:46.240
Hatter.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:49.520
Queen.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:53.060
Cheshire.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:55.900
And...

00:05:57.650 --> 00:05:58.560
Alice.

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.270
I love the all-black look!

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:06.630
Great! Staying up three 
straight nights was worth it!

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.390
Yay for all black!

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:10.640
What's the matter, Alice?

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:13.000
This is a lot of padding.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.140
Yuzu, do you like large breasts?

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:19.100
Lar— N-No! I'm not into that at all!

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:23.670
Maybe that's why you like milk. 
It comes from cow teats, after all.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:27.110
Will you listen to me? It's Yana 
who likes that kind of thing!

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:28.720
Yana-san does?

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:32.610
So Yana-san likes them bigger.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:34.360
Yeah, that's right.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:35.980
You can't go wrong by going bigger.

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:39.620
On that note, Yuzu, we've got 
height-increasing shoes for you.

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:45.410
Wouldn't it be a problem if 
Alice were taller than you?

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:49.220
Huh?

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:52.090
The person you like is Kiryuu Momo?

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:52.990
Yes.

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:56.580
The guy who writes music for Baby?

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:57.940
The really famous songwriter?

00:06:57.940 --> 00:06:58.540
Yes.

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:02.110
So that means Kiryuu Momo 
is only 16 or 17 years old?!

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:03.140
Seriously?

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:03.910
Yes.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:09.070
How are you so calm after getting 
hold of hot intel like that?

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:13.370
Apparently, Momo won't come 
to my audition, and only mine.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:15.650
Really? Why?

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:17.350
I don't know!

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:18.370
Oh!

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:21.140
But I'll sing anyway.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.340
I'll sing to reach him.

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:27.520
Well, okay, I guess...

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.460
I'll take a look at him for you, then.

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:33.800
I went to the same audition, 
and I made it through.

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:35.530
I see.

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:39.810
Then can you check his tummy for 
a birthmark and his butt for a burn?

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:42.590
If he has both of those, it's definitely him.

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:46.260
Can you not say that as if you're just 
asking me to pick up some soy sauce?

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:48.090
You're setting the bar way too high.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:50.690
But anyway, I guess I'll 
just have to do my best.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:56.200
Miou.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.700
I became In NO Hurry's Alice.

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:03.050
I know.

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:05.710
Haruyoshi-senpai told me.

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:18.890
Alice. Going home?

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:19.620
Yeah.

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:20.490
To Hase Station?

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:21.070
Yeah.

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:23.490
I just happen to have something to do at Hase!

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.800
<i>I guess I'll just have to do my best...</i>

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:35.780
Hase

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:33.700
So, tomorrow's the day. May 29th.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.550
You've been practicing every day. 
It must've been hard on you.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:39.180
No, not at all.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:41.250
I was happy.

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:43.870
Because I got to sing your songs.

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:07.150
Same. I was happy to have you 
closer to me than ever before.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:09.710
Did you say something?

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:12.530
No! I didn't say a word!

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:14.990
I'll be waiting for you 
at the studio tomorrow!

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:18.810
Right. Tomorrow's the day, Yuzu.

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:20.290
I'm looking forward to it.

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:24.820
<i>It's so strange.</i>

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:27.830
<i>I'm going to appear on TV,</i>

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:29.760
<i>and I'll be singing as Alice...</i>

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:32.130
<i>And...</i>

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:34.130
Just sing.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:37.430
It's not bad, you're not a nuisance, 
and it's not annoying.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:39.790
You're fine just the way you are.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:43.210
<i>On the same day,</i>

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:44.940
<i>I'll be singing</i>

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:48.440
<i>closer to Momo than I have in six years.</i>

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:54.740
Hey.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.450
Where are we running to, anyway?

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:58.860
Say something, Mom!

00:09:58.250 --> 00:09:59.950
Fasten your seat belt.

00:10:03.110 --> 00:10:04.860
So what are you going to do?

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:08.210
Do you even have anywhere to go?

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:10.710
Answer me!

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:15.960
So you're not listening? Just like Nino.

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:27.830
Nino...

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:34.910
I'm coming in.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:39.470
I brought coffee.

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:42.990
You look pale.

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:44.570
Are you okay?

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:47.940
I had a dream about my past.

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:49.740
About Nino-chan?

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:58.170
The songs you had written when we 
first met were for her, weren't they?

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:02.830
I wanted Nino to sing them one day.

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:06.630
But I used them all for work.

00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:12.480
For money.

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:19.000
I can't even remember how to 
write songs for her anymore.

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:21.710
Mother

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:24.850
Sorry.

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:27.140
<i>When's the next deposit?</i>

00:11:28.030 --> 00:11:29.080
This weekend.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:31.420
<i>I see. So you have work?</i>

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:32.900
<i>Are you doing a good job?</i>

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.660
<i>You are making decent money, right?</i>

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:36.090
Yeah.

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:38.390
<i>That's good to hear.</i>

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:42.270
<i>I'm really happy.</i>

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:45.280
<i>Who would have thought 
you had this kind of talent?</i>

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:46.600
<i>I'm really proud of you.</i>

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:50.890
<i>You loved to sing, didn't you? 
Even though you're tone-deaf.</i>

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:52.590
<i>Do you remember?</i>

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:54.620
<i>You used to sing every night 
with Nino-chan next door—</i>

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:56.220
Don't say her name!

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:57.880
Damn it!

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:10.130
Nino is the one person

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:14.040
I don't want seeing me like this.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.550
Audition Area

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.550
Vocalist Audition 
Be produced by Kiryuu Momo

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:28.690
All right, time to belt one out there, Nino.

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:29.340
Yeah.

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:34.190
I'll leave Momo's tummy birthmark 
and butt burn to you.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:36.170
Don't push it.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:38.600
Let's go.

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.700
I'll be calling you in order.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:48.570
Please enter the audition area 
in the order I call your name.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:51.480
Number 1, Tanada-san.

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:52.000
Yes.

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:54.010
<i>It's strange.</i>

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:56.250
<i>I know Momo's in that room right now.</i>

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:59.370
<i>So why am I so calm?</i>

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:05.520
<i>It must be because I know exactly where 
Momo is now, and what he's doing.</i>

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:08.260
You have to believe you'll see 
him again and keep singing.

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:11.140
Believe you'll reach him and keep singing.

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:16.150
If you do that, I'm sure you'll 
see him someday, in some way.

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:20.020
Number 10, Arisugawa-san. Come in.

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:39.480
I'm number 10, Arisugawa Nino.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:42.210
I will sing <i>Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star</i>.

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:52.220
<i>Twinkle, twinkle, little star</i>

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:57.100
<i>How I wonder what you are</i>

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:02.110
<i>Up above the world so high</i>

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.560
<i>Momo isn't here right now.</i>

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:06.490
<i>Like a diamond in the sky</i>

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:05.030
<i>But...</i>

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:11.620
Even if he doesn't go, as long as you 
audition, Momo will have to listen, right?

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:11.620
<i>Twinkle, twinkle, little star</i>

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:16.140
<i>How I wonder what you are</i>

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.710
<i>I'll believe in those words</i>

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:16.500
<i>and leave my song here.</i>

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:21.270
<i>Twinkle, twinkle, little star</i>

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:21.510
<i>Listen to me, Momo.</i>

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:25.880
<i>How I wonder what you are</i>

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:30.880
<i>And I hope that our song</i>

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:35.640
<i>Will reach out to everyone</i>

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:40.020
<i>Twinkle, twinkle, little star</i>

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:00.970
Mo... mo?

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:05.460
Sorry, but can you wait here for me?

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:11.340
Alice.

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:16.850
Mo... mo?

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:22.470
Did she say "Momo" just now?

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:24.480
What? Do you know her, Kiryuu?

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:26.980
Hey, Kiryuu!

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:29.240
Momo...

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:30.570
Wait, Momo!

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:32.090
Momo!

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:37.040
Momo!

00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:42.370
Momo-kun!

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:46.130
Let's sing!

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:57.560
You fail.

00:15:58.770 --> 00:15:59.550
Get out.

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:04.150
I can't make money with your song.

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:06.610
You fail, Nino.

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:13.000
What does that mean?

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:16.740
What are you saying?!

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:19.660
I didn't sing all this time for that!

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:21.960
I sang because I believed in what you said!

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:24.220
Because I wanted to see you!

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:26.950
Aren't you the one who said

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:30.520
you hoped that we could use my song 
as a guide to see each other again?

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:31.950
Momo!

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:39.890
Uh... Arisugawa-san, um...

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:42.130
Thank you very much.

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:43.640
Excuse me.

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:47.670
What was that?

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:49.570
Who knows?

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:52.700
It's time.

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:57.360
I have to go to <i>Music King</i>.

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:04.100
You fail.

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:07.520
I can't make money with your song.

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:09.110
<i>Momo.</i>

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:11.330
<i>Momo.</i>

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:12.760
<i>Momo.</i>

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:13.840
<i>Momo.</i>

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:15.180
<i>Momo.</i>

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:16.680
Alice!

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:19.180
I'm glad you're here.

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:21.680
I was kind of worried, so I came to get—

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:44.290
So you met him.

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:45.940
Momo.

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:50.240
<i>Just moments ago, my throat 
was singing so happily.</i>

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:53.260
<i>But now it hurts so much, like it's on fire.</i>

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:57.220
Alice.

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:06.520
Please take us to K Studio.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:18.570
<i>Momo.</i>

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:20.780
<i>Momo.</i>

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:23.790
<i>Momo.</i>

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:28.310
<i>I wanted to see you again all this time!</i>

00:18:30.470 --> 00:18:32.540
So we're decided, then.

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:34.920
Good work, everyone.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:41.490
You said you weren't going 
to Nino-chan's audition.

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:42.510
You surprised me.

00:18:43.660 --> 00:18:46.520
Right before it started,
you suddenly decided to go.

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:49.520
It's my job, so I thought I'd better.

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:51.190
Aren't you going to the party?

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:54.030
No. I'll work instead.

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:57.600
Looking like that?

00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:01.620
<i>Nino.</i>

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:03.330
<i>I didn't want to see you.</i>

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:05.330
<i>But...</i>

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:08.940
<i>I always wanted to see you.</i>

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:12.710
Now's the time you've all been waiting for!

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:15.750
The super popular band,

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:18.380
In NO Hurry to Shout, finally 
makes an appearance on stage!

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:21.210
All right, go get 'em!

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:22.140
Got it!

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:22.140
Okay.

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:27.280
In NO Hurry has been growing steadily in 
popularity since their debut a year ago.

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:31.900
It's what you've all been waiting for, 
their first TV appearance!

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:31.900
<i>Please.</i>

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:36.400
<i>Endure it.</i>

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:37.900
<i>Focus.</i>

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.950
<i>I'll end up like I did at the school concert.</i>

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:45.430
Without further ado, 
let's hear their performance.

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:45.870
<i>Everything. Everything.</i>

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:48.730
This is their new single to be included on 
their first album coming out this August.

00:19:48.090 --> 00:19:49.160
<i>Sing it all out.</i>

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:50.750
"Canary"!

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:54.800
<i>I've made up my mind.</i>

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:59.670
<i>I will definitely make you look my way.</i>

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:04.930
<i>Fly!</i>

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:15.060
<i>Whether I'm awake or asleep</i>

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:17.480
<i>I'm nothing more then a canary</i>

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:22.360
<i>Inside a sweet, glistening cage of ideals</i>

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:25.410
<i>Whether I'm awake or asleep</i>

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:26.190
<i>This is bad. Alice is going berserk again.</i>

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:27.530
<i>I can't leave my cage</i>

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:32.800
<i>I'm always there when I wake up</i>

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:30.540
<i>It's okay.</i>

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:34.620
<i>I can keep up.</i>

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:38.590
<i>You say that's fine if everyone's here</i>

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:39.050
<i>Really, our little canary is going wild.</i>

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:42.680
<i>So come here with me</i>

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:41.860
<i>We'll catch you this time, though!</i>

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:46.020
<i>She's rushing even more than 
at the school performance.</i>

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:48.960
<i>When I shout, that alone makes me invincible</i>

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:49.390
But unlike then, she's 
listening to us this time.

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:52.720
<i>So please don't open this cage</i>

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:50.870
<i>This...</i>

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:53.770
<i>might work!</i>

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:57.770
<i>I'll fall</i>

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:03.870
<i>Straight down</i>

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:05.870
<i>It's not enough.</i>

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:07.470
<i>Not enough! Not enough!</i>

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:09.000
<i>I won't reach him like this!</i>

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:11.410
<i>More.</i>

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:12.450
<i>More.</i>

00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:14.590
<i>More!</i>

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:21.550
Hey... Momo, what are you doing?

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:22.460
Is your guitar okay?

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:28.100
Momo?

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:29.930
Nino.

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:35.100
<i>What is this?</i>

00:21:41.630 --> 00:21:42.860
<i>She's a monster.</i>

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:48.040
<i>Even if I'm completely naked,
I'm not scared anymore</i>

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:51.940
<i>I'll keep on singing, because I'm a canary</i>

00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:02.000
<i>I regretted it.</i>

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:04.010
<i>Back then,</i>

00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:06.750
<i>if I had stopped you when you went berserk,</i>

00:22:11.780 --> 00:22:15.660
<i>I wouldn't have had to 
see you smile like that.</i>

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:52.320
♭06 
Today and Tomorrow, I'll Walk
